            <ArticleTitle>[Singular diaphragm-like colonic stricture and short-term administration of a non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drug].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>525-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of diaphragm-like stricture of the colon induced by non steroidal anti-inflammatory drug (diclofénac LP) is reported in a 65-year-old man who presented abdominal pain. Colonoscopy revealed ulcer in the transverse right colon. The patient gradually developed diaphragm-like stricture in the transverse right colon. A right hemicolectomy was performed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
